Provenance and attribution for the vendored source in this directory.

WHAT THIS IS
  A vendored copy of the RandomX engine plus a WebAssembly JIT backend, taken
  from https://github.com/aa022/RandomX-bonanza (commit f9848e3, 2026-10-02).
  It is the port base for the browser miner's hash-rate work: upstream RandomX
  gates RANDOMX_HAVE_COMPILER to x86-64/aarch64/riscv64, so wasm32 lands on
  JitCompilerFallback and our current build runs the interpreter only. This tree
  adds a wasm backend that emits WebAssembly at runtime and lets the browser's
  own JIT compile it.

WHY WE VENDOR RATHER THAN PATCH
  Our previous tree was WebRandomX (a different fork) plus patches, including a
  thread-local fix for softfloat's process-global FP rounding mode. This tree
  does not use softfloat at all -- rx_vec_f128 is __m128d, i.e. wasm SIMD
  doubles -- so that hazard does not exist here and the patch is not needed.
  Taking this tree as the base and re-applying our small API shim is far less
  work, and far less risk, than porting ~1,360 changed lines across 14 core
  files into our old tree.

